.TH geectl-local-build-chroot 1  "geectl-local-build-chroot 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-local\-build\-chroot \- Enter the preserved build root of the last build for the package and run repro commands there, read from stdin, one per line, joined with `&&` into one shell command. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` runs the commands in the root. A terminal on stdin is refused instead of blocking on a read that never arrives. A failing repro still exits 0: the exit code is data, in `exit:` and in `record.result.exit_code`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl local\-build chroot\fR [\fB\-\-arch\fR] [\fB\-\-flavor\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\-secs\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-project\fR> <\fB\-\-repo\fR> <\fIDIRECTORY\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Enter the preserved build root of the last build for the package and run repro commands there, read from stdin, one per line, joined with `&&` into one shell command. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` runs the commands in the root. A terminal on stdin is refused instead of blocking on a read that never arrives. A failing repro still exits 0: the exit code is data, in `exit:` and in `record.result.exit_code`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
The OBS project the package belongs to
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<REPO>\fR
The repository the root was built for (e.g. `standard`)
.TP
\fB\-\-arch\fR \fI<ARCH>\fR
The architecture the root was built for; defaults to the host arch
.TP
\fB\-\-flavor\fR \fI<FLAVOR>\fR
The multibuild flavor; required when the source carries a `_multibuild` file
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\-secs\fR \fI<TIMEOUT_SECS>\fR [default: 3600]
Timeout in seconds for the whole run
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIDIRECTORY\fR>
The source directory (spec + sources); the package comes from the spec file in it, like the build
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
